# Future work tracking

When work is **deferred**, **out of scope for the current task**, or **discovered during implementation**, record it so it is not lost. Pick the right doc — do not default to chat-only notes.

**Canonical sources:**

- [docs/FRD.md](../../docs/FRD.md) — product roadmap (**Today** / **Planned**)
- [docs/TECH-DEBT.md](../../docs/TECH-DEBT.md) — bugs, quality gaps, fix-up and investigation items

## Decide where it goes

| Track in **FRD** (Planned) | Track in **TECH-DEBT** (Open) |
|---|---|
| New capability users would choose or notice | Known bug or regression |
| Intentional product direction | Existing behavior that should work but does not meet quality bar |
| New vial size, mode, template, account layer, etc. | Print/export quality vs real hardware (padding, crispness, DPI mismatch) |
| “We will build X later” as a feature | Refactor, cleanup, or investigation follow-up |
| Changes **what** the product offers | Fixes **how well** shipped behavior works |

**Examples:**

- Landing page, calculator-only mode, 10 ml vial → **FRD** Planned
- Export margin too large on B21, text less crisp than native Niimbot text → **TECH-DEBT**
- Shipped print setup but missing first-run wizard polish → usually **TECH-DEBT** unless it is a committed product milestone

## When unclear

If the item could reasonably be **roadmap** or **fix-up**, **ask the developer** (or the user) which doc to use before adding it. Briefly state both options and your lean.

Do not duplicate the same item in both docs unless the user explicitly wants both angles (rare — avoid by default).

## When adding an entry

- **FRD:** value-led **why + what**; match existing Planned tone (see `functional-requirements.mdc`).
- **TECH-DEBT:** symptom, priority, status, and concrete hypotheses or files to inspect.
- On the same change set when you **ship** the fix: move TECH-DEBT items to **Resolved**; move FRD items from **Planned** to **Today**.
